    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="76593d58-e99b-5f43-a125-ce9cf40852a7" activityNameId="e887ef85-00c6-5325-943c-520dfe61c4ca" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Reinforcing steel, import to CH</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Reinforcing steel, import to CH
Represents Swiss import mix of reinforced steel. Based on data from the swiss steel association 100% of the import is steel from secondary material. The European country percentages were calculated using the five‑year average from Swiss import‑customs data.

Distribution: Germany 32 %, France 42 %, Italy 55 %, Poland 3.5 %, and for the remaining 5.3 % the RER process was used.

For each country the transportation was modelled using information from the swiss steel association. Which resulted in the following: DE 670 km (14% lorry, 86% train), FR 540 km lorry, IT 425 km lorry, PL 1400 km lorry and RER was averaged to 1643.3 km lorry (Average from remaining countries).  
UUID: 359ffce6-23b6-3ee0-a57b-6a8dd6712f85
Location: Data from literature, referring to Europe and Switzerland
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 
Sampling: Data from literature
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_359ffce6-23b6-3ee0-a57b-6a8dd6712f85.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
